Ark Ceremony Recap | 13/10

Last night's Ark Ceremony gave me more reasons to stay curious about what Arkadian is building. There are exciting developments behind the scenes, and I think the next stage will be worth watching.

1. Coops and a Potential Compute Opportunity

@wujir0  is back in Marchville, where he attended college, for a conference with people whose net worths are estimated at $400–500 million. Many come from real estate backgrounds and are highly interested in AI. He shared a photo of a meal with them and has connected with the Dean of Marchville, with the goal of supplying them with compute. This is significant alpha, and a big thank you to Coops for all the hard work happening behind the scenes.

2. A Treasure Hunt Has Begun

Something has already been shared on the internet and brought to the Mods' attention. If someone in the community finds it, they will earn an Ingot. This is a real treasure hunt, and the hunt has officially begun. There are also many big things coming to Arkadian, so stay tuned!

3. Community Recognition and Feedback

Mod @BlockBeaconn  took the stage to recognize active community members and those who earned an Ingot for their activity over the past week. @lon_rong14459  was among them and also earned the @I'm Onboard role.

The team is also looking for genuine feedback on Pocket Socrates, Arts, and Posts/Articles. If you have useful suggestions, share them with any of the @grovekeepers. Valid feedback and suggestions will be rewarded.

4. Antislop Progress

@Adeimantos shared that the team is still improving the AI rewrite feature because it doesn't catch all the slop yet. The payment and usage-limit layers have been successfully developed, and the overall product has improved. The rewrite feature still has some hiccups, but once those are fixed, it is expected to become one of the best AI rewrite tools on the market.

Another interesting development was hinted at: AI Proofer, an engine designed to improve the rewrite system for users. More details will be shared on the official Antislop X account: https://t.co/RbFHVDF1gj

Also, shout-out to @🦋Sarah | Ify for creating a jingle for Antislop!

5. Arkadian AI Product Direction
Arkadian AI is looking for AI API consumers, ideally production-grade applications that will actively use AI, such as Antislop or Pocket Socrates. There was also some general discussion about different AI models.

For me, it's interesting to see the focus on real applications and actual AI usage, alongside the ongoing product improvements. There is still work to do, but these updates give us more to follow as Arkadian continues to develop.
